WEBVTT
TITLE The Buddy System: Orders, the XOR Buddy Rule, Splits, Merge Cascades and Both Fragmentations — GATE Visual Explainer
NOTE Timings are estimated from the lesson timeline (speaking-rate based), not measured from recorded audio.

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.500
A request must receive one contiguous run of memory, not scattered pieces.

2
00:00:07.500 --> 00:00:15.000
Halve the pool again and again, and every block has exactly one partner: its other half.

3
00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:22.500
A pool of 64 units has 127 blocks in its tree: 64 of size 1 up to 1 of size 64.

4
00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:30.000
The partner is found by arithmetic, not by a search: flip one bit of the address.

5
00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:37.500
Request 13 units. Round up to the next power of two: 16.

6
00:00:37.500 --> 00:00:45.000
Three splits: 128 into 64, 64 into 32, 32 into 16.

7
00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:52.500
The exam answer: 16 units, 3 splits, and 3 units of internal fragmentation.

8
00:00:52.500 --> 00:01:00.000
The 112 units left are not lost: three blocks of 16, 32 and 64, all free.

9
00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:07.500
The buddy of a block is its address XOR its size.

10
00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:15.000
Address 24, size 8: 24 XOR 8 is 16, because only bit 3 differs.

11
00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:22.500
All 126 blocks of a 64-unit pool pass: each pair forms exactly one parent.

12
00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:30.000
XOR twice returns the address, so the rule is symmetric and free is fast.

13
00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:37.500
One free list per order. A request looks at its own order, then one order up.

14
00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:45.000
In 1024 units: 50, 150, 90, 130, 70 and 80 are served, with 6 splits and 960 out.

15
00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:52.500
The seventh request, 120 units, fails: no 128 exists, though 64 units are free.

16
00:01:52.500 --> 00:02:00.000
The requests 180 and 68 fail as well, and a failed request changes nothing.

17
00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:07.500
Four requests of 8 units: addresses 0, 8, 16 and 24, with 4 splits in total.

18
00:02:07.500 --> 00:02:15.000
Freeing address 0 merges nothing: its buddy, address 8, is still allocated.

19
00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:22.500
Freeing 8 then merges once into a 16 at 0; freeing 16 does nothing at all.

20
00:02:22.500 --> 00:02:30.000
Freeing 24 cascades three times: to 16, to 32, then to the whole 64.

21
00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:37.500
Internal fragmentation is the block minus the request: 16 minus 13 is 3.

22
00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:45.000
The worst case is just over half a block: 33 units take 64 and waste 31.

23
00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:52.500
The waste is always under half, and exactly zero for a power-of-two request.

24
00:02:52.500 --> 00:03:00.000
Uniform requests from 1 to 64 waste 22.3 per cent; the published range is 25 to 33.

25
00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:07.500
Four blocks of 16 at 0, 16, 32 and 48, then free the second and the fourth.

26
00:03:07.500 --> 00:03:15.000
32 units are free, in two blocks of 16 — and 16 and 48 are not buddies.

27
00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:22.500
A request for 32 fails. This is external fragmentation, and buddy has it.

28
00:03:22.500 --> 00:03:30.000
Merging joins halves of one parent, so a free neighbour is not enough.

29
00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:37.500
Buddy gives one contiguous run; paging gives scattered frames.

30
00:03:37.500 --> 00:03:45.000
So buddy has both fragmentations; paging wastes only inside the last page.

31
00:03:45.000 --> 00:03:52.500
The Fibonacci variant uses 1, 2, 3, 5, 8 instead of powers of two.

32
00:03:52.500 --> 00:04:00.000
Real kernels layer a slab allocator on top to cut the internal waste.

33
00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:07.500
Five shapes: which request fails, the size and splits, the free lists, the buddy, the merges.

34
00:04:07.500 --> 00:04:15.000
For which request fails, simulate and stop at the first failure.

35
00:04:15.000 --> 00:04:22.500
For size and splits: round up, then count the halvings from the pool order down.

36
00:04:22.500 --> 00:04:30.000
For the buddy, XOR the address with the size; for merges, cascade while the buddy is free.

37
00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:37.500
Trap 1: a buddy is not a neighbour. 16 and 48 sit in one free list and are not buddies.

38
00:04:37.500 --> 00:04:45.000
Trap 2: half means half of the block, never half of the pool.

39
00:04:45.000 --> 00:04:52.500
Trap 3: rounding down. A request for 13 units never receives 8.

40
00:04:52.500 --> 00:05:00.000
Trap 4: no external fragmentation is false. 32 free units can refuse a 32-unit request.

